## A thin vertical blocker standing on a horizontal
## floor, its base at gap 0.001, lit at near-grazing incidence --
## towardLight makes 86.57 degrees with the floor's own normal (sinTheta
## 0.9982) -- from the side. A narrow fov (6 degrees) magnifies the floor
## strip beside the blocker's base: a magnitude-scaled bias would leak a
## band there 1e-2*sinTheta*Yres/(2*tan(fov/2)) =
## 1e-2*0.9982*480/(2*tan(3deg)) =~ 46 px wide, comfortably above the
## 10 px a per-pixel comparison needs to resolve. This overrides AGENTS.md's
## default camera for this fixture, on r5b_quadrics.rib's own precedent.
## contactshadow_noblocker.rib is this scene with the blocker removed. Not
## third-party.
Display "contactshadow.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 640 480 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [6]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.1]
LightSource "distantlight" 2 "intensity" [15.0] "lightcolor" [1 1 1]
	"from" [50 3 0] "to" [0 0 0]
Surface "matte" "Ka" [0.2] "Kd" [0.8]

Polygon "P" [-0.5 -0.05 -3  -0.5 -0.05 3  0.5 -0.05 3  0.5 -0.05 -3]

AttributeBegin
	Polygon "P" [0.1 -0.049 -3  0.1 -0.049 3  0.1 0.051 3  0.1 0.051 -3]
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
